## Why This Is Asked
Tests data residency, tenant isolation, and end-to-end security in real-time inference.

## Key Concepts
- PrivateLink isolation and per-tenant KMS envelopes
- Tenant-scoped Feature Store and de-identification
- Canary rollouts and drift monitoring
- Rollback criteria and latency targets

## Code Example
```javascript
// Pseudo preprocessor: drop PII, hash identifiers
function preprocess(input, tenantId){
  const deid = deidentify(input);
  const keys = kms.getTenantKey(tenantId);
  return envelopeEncrypt(deid, keys);
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you test per-tenant key rotation without service interruption?
- What metrics would you use to trigger automatic rollbacks?
- How would you handle cross-tenant model version drift detection?

## Why This Is Asked
Tests experience building production ML pipelines in AWS with strict data locality, latency targets, and privacy. Assesses ability to combine PrivateLink, Lake Formation, Feature Store, canary deployment, drift monitoring, and cost governance.

## Key Concepts
- SageMaker PrivateLink
- Lake Formation data access
- Feature Store
- Endpoint traffic splitting (canary)
- Drift detection & retraining triggers
- DP privacy controls and encryption

## Code Example
```javascript
// Example drift score calculation (KS statistic placeholder)
function ksDrift(p, q) {
  let max = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < p.length; i++) {
    max = Math.max(max, Math.abs(p[i] - q[i]));
  }
  return max;
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How would you rollback if canary drift triggers fire?
- What metrics and thresholds would you alert on for latency, FP rate, and drift?
